  "note": "Complete permanent Edinburgh Waverley station exterior: full mapped pitched/glazed five-row roof field with central opening,western classical entrance pavilions and descending links,all six internal stone passenger/service ranges,central booking-hall rooflight,long arched Market Street stone frontage,upper street office,curved glass entrance pavilion and two descending glazed stair roofs. Preserve independent Waverley Market,Balmoral/other hotels,bridges,roads,rails andplatform space. No trains,buses,brands,sculptures or navigable interiors. Native8m booking/eastern ranges and5m narrow range remain map facts. Source lower floor+.65m,upper street entrances+7.5m,main pitched-roof eaves9.5m/crowns11.5–13.5m,main booking hall8m/rooflight10.2m and Market Street office20m. Unknown small-range roofs use5.5m/6m. The source deliberately models upper-street to lower-station connections rather than placing every floor at one height. Exact rail floor and historic threshold elevations remain approximate. One unchanged standard host sample outside the eastern station roof,local[315,10], 52.695071999999996m supplies one common datum. Source foundations/support feet-6m,lower occupied floor+.65m andupper entry floors+7.5m. No per-part host offsets or artificial surrounding plaza. The prepared urban field rises over the lower station and must be reviewed explicitly;the rounded63m grid-center sample isnot a lower-platform datum. Preview uses the host terrain sample at the authored base; ground slope, facade azimuth and final site fit remain review items."
